can be taken into the margin, provided</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; it is conspicuously =
wider than the text;&nbsp; but if it is done</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; more than once, the =
larger illustrations should all be of the</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; same =
width.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \\</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \dots\ metal blocks =
\dots\ flanges of about 1/8 in \dots\ \\</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Half-tone =
illustrations \dots\ illustration area in harmony with</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; the type area \dots =
\\</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \dots\ undesirable to =
lay down a set of rules \dots\ But a few \lq\lq</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;rules</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; of thumb&quot; are =
helpful \dots \\</FONT>

<BR><FONT SIZE=3D2>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If two pictures are to =
